  "class_profile_rule": {
    "one_profile_per_class": "Each class a character possesses has its own Martial Practice, Spellcraft, and Psionic Discipline values. Multiclass characters share one CEP bank and one 500-point increase limit across all class profiles at each level-up.",
    "base_class_lock": "Axis movement changes the active path inside the class. It does not replace the selected base class or its common chassis. Optional full class retraining should be handled as a separate campaign project.",
    "path_features": "At a confirmed path change, old path-specific features become dormant and the matching path features up to the character’s current class level become active. Base class features remain. Dormant features cannot be used, stacked, or harvested for permanent benefits.",
    "progression": "Use only the active path’s spell-slot, psionic-grade, Focus, and path-feature progression. Never combine the half, full, and hybrid progressions at once.",
    "gear_transition": "Training changes permission, not inventory. Crossing a Martial Practice threshold does not create gear. When training falls, currently worn gear remains physically present, but proficiency becomes dormant after the confirming Haven Rest unless another feature supplies it."
